## Why it's split

This repository is mostly not this project's own work: it mirrors figures
published by the Japanese government and other public bodies, and it
reproduces the text of Japanese statutes. Applying one license to the whole
repository would misstate rights this project doesn't hold. So the license is
split by what's actually being licensed.

**Code** (LICENSE, MIT) — the HTML/CSS/JS and build scripts that make the site
run.

**Data and text** (LICENSE-DATA, CC BY 4.0) — the parts this project made.
That includes, but is not limited to: which indicators were chosen and how
they're arranged; the annotations and the classification of each review
clause's status; the mapping from each figure to its primary-source URL; the
written prose (About page, per-page descriptions, etc.); and the images made
for this site under `assets/`.

**Not licensed by this project, because it isn't this project's to license:**

- The individual government/public-body figures themselves. Facts are not
  subject to copyright.
- The full text of Japanese statutes under `data/hoan_clauses/*.txt`. Under
  Article 13 of Japan's Copyright Act, laws and regulations are excluded from
  copyright protection outright.
- The underlying primary sources (government publications, PDFs, Diet
  proceedings, etc.). Rights to those belong to whoever published them.

## A note on the lists

The lists above name what's most likely to be asked about. They are examples,
not an exhaustive inventory — something not named is not thereby excluded. The
dividing line is authorship, not enumeration: what this project wrote or
compiled is CC BY 4.0, and what it merely mirrors is not this project's to
license. If a specific file's status matters to you and isn't clear from that
rule, ask via https://zurekei.org/contact rather than guessing.

Third-party components: this site loads the IBM Plex fonts from the Google
Fonts CDN at runtime. No copy of those fonts is redistributed in this
repository, so their license is not implicated here.
